<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · concept</p><h1 class="enc-title">Franco-Mongol alliance</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Franco-Mongol alliance refers to attempts in the thirteenth and early fourteenth centuries to coordinate action between the Mongol <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a> and Christian European rulers and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">papacy</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluks</a>. Embassies were exchanged, but the efforts never produced effective military cooperation.</p></div>
